# Surface and near-surface creatures: what you meet before you start digging.
#
# READ THE NUMBERS IN THE PLAYER'S FRAME. speed/jumpSpeed/gravityScale are
# authored as if this creature were the 24px reference character the player's
# physics were tuned against; src/entities/mobs/MobDefs.ts multiplies them by
# PHYS_SCALE * (bodyCellsH * CELL / PLAYER_H) at load. So `speed 110` here means
# "about a third of the player's MAX_RUN_SPEED 360, relative to its own body",
# and it stays true if movement is ever retuned. Radii (aggroPx, fleePx,
# ranged.range) are NOT scaled — they are about how far away something notices
# you on screen, which is a property of the camera, not of its legs.
# Full rationale: tools/contentc/schema/mob.ts.
#
# ART: one character is one WORLD CELL. A pose is one `art.seq` record whose
# heredoc body holds every frame of that loop, frames separated by a blank line.
# Sizes run 2x2 to 4x3 cells (10x10 to 20x15 px) against a 2x3 player — the
# range where a creature reads as a creature at a 5px cell.
#
# BODY vs ART. bodyCellsW/bodyCellsH are the collision box and the body-scale
# anchor; art.cellsW/art.cellsH are only how big the picture is. No bodyCells*
# value was touched by the art pass, which is what `npm run verify:mobs` asserts.
#
# The pads have since landed: MobDefs.ts derives `wPx`/`hPx` from bodyCells* and
# `artWPx`/`artHPx`/`artPadXPx`/`artPadTopPx` from the sprite, so art may now
# overhang the body — horns, wings, a plume — without widening the hitbox. Every
# creature here still keeps the two EQUAL, because the redraw predated the pads
# and staying square was the conservative choice; growing one is now a pure art
# edit. Two rules the facade enforces at load: art may never be SMALLER than the
# body in either axis (that is a hole in the hitbox), and artCellsW - bodyCellsW
# must be even, or the centred pad puts sprite pixels half a cell off the grid.
#
# ---- WHAT THE PLAY MODES BOUGHT --------------------------------------------
# Every pose used to be `loop`, so an idle was a two-frame twitch and a jump was
# the same two frames going round forever. The vocabulary is now:
#
#   ambient  IDLE. frames[0..n-2] alternate as a breath; the LAST frame is an
#            interrupt held for `blinkFor` every `blinkEvery`. That last frame
#            is used as a TELL wherever a creature has one — the sentinel's
#            optic going red, the bladeframe's edge lighting up, the moth
#            flaring before it spits. A player who watches the room now gets
#            warning, and it cost no code.
#   phase    GROUND LOCOMOTION. Indexed by real horizontal speed instead of by
#            wall-clock, so a creature that has a chaseSpeed does not keep
#            patrol-rate legs while it charges. Four frames, contacts on the
#            first and third, exactly like the player's run.
#   loop     Anything whose rhythm is genuinely its own and not its feet: wing
#            beats, a swim undulation, a hopper's shuffle.
#   once     AIR, on anything that leaves the ground under its own power —
#            launch, then the apex frame is HELD until it lands.
#   hold     AIR on things that only ever fall, and any pose that is one frame.
#
# NO `fps=` ON AN IDLE, ANYWHERE. The facade halves the idle rate for every
# creature at once; setting a rate here to compensate would bake that decision
# into 21 files. `art.fps` is tuned so both the full-rate move and the halved
# idle read, and that is the only rate knob these files touch.

# --- Grubling ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Armoured surface crawler. The baseline hostile: slow patrol, real charge,
# short notice radius, so it is a threat you walk into rather than one that
# hunts you across a field. Its chitin is the first armour the player meets.
@mob grubling
name          Grubling
brain         walker
maxHealth     14
contactDamage 8
armor         1
bodyCellsW    2
bodyCellsH    2
speed         110
chaseSpeed    215
aggroPx       130
aggroYPx      40
beat          2.4
blood         #a9753d
xp            4
value         2
drops         item=chitin count=1..2
drops         item=grub_meat count=1 chance=35%
bands         surface shallow
biomes        plains savanna jungle swamp tundra desert
weight        26

# Four pixels, so the shell IS the creature: row 0 is plate, row 1 is legs, and
# every frame differs only in which of those two is doing something. The added
# ink tone (1) pulls the legs out of the shell colour they used to share, which
# is what makes the two rows read as two different materials at this size.
art.cellsW 2
art.cellsH 2
art.pal    . #3a2617 #6f4a2a #a9753d #ffd27a
art.fps    7
art.seq  state=idle mode=ambient blinkEvery=3.4 blinkFor=0.14 |
  23
  11

  22
  11

  34
  11
art.seq  state=move mode=phase |
  23
  1.

  23
  11

  23
  .1

  23
  11
# No jumpSpeed, so this pose only ever means "walked off something".
art.seq  state=air mode=hold |
  23
  ..

# --- Critter ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Small, bright, harmless, panics. fleePx (not aggroPx) is what flips the walker
# brain into running away; the very high chaseSpeed is its bolt, not a charge.
# It exists to make a meadow feel occupied and to be the thing you chase for
# hide, so it is worth nothing to fight and something to catch.
@mob critter
name          Critter
brain         skitter
maxHealth     6
contactDamage 0
bodyCellsW    2
bodyCellsH    2
speed         120
chaseSpeed    330
jumpSpeed     560
fleePx        105
beat          1.6
blood         #f2e3c8
xp            1
drops         item=hide count=1 chance=60%
bands         surface
biomes        plains savanna jungle swamp tundra glacier
weight        22

# Head high, body low: column 0 of row 0 is EMPTY in most frames, which is the
# whole silhouette — a small thing with its head up. The ear coming up (frame 1
# of the idle) and the nose flaring pink (the interrupt) are the only two things
# a two-by-two prey animal can say, and they are both alarm.
art.cellsW 2
art.cellsH 2
art.pal    . #3a2c22 #c8b7a0 #f2e3c8 #ff9a9a
art.fps    12
art.seq  state=idle mode=ambient blinkEvery=2.6 blinkFor=0.12 |
  .3
  22

  23
  22

  .4
  22
art.seq  state=move mode=phase |
  .3
  12

  .3
  22

  .3
  21

  .3
  22
# A bound, not a fall: launch with the feet already gone, then the stretched
# apex is held until it lands.
art.seq  state=air mode=once fps=14 |
  .3
  22

  23
  .2

# --- Sandworm ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Travels inside the rock line and erupts. The long beat is the whole design:
# a burrower that surfaced often would just be a walker with a worse silhouette.
# Restricted to loose ground (sand, savanna hardpan, snow, ice) because a worm
# swimming through granite reads as a bug rather than as a creature.
@mob sandworm
name          Sandworm
brain         burrower
maxHealth     30
contactDamage 16
attackCooldown 1
armor         2
bodyCellsW    4
bodyCellsH    2
speed         150
chaseSpeed    210
jumpSpeed     700
aggroPx       190
aggroYPx      110
beat          2.8
blood         #c39a5a
xp            12
value         6
drops         item=worm_hide count=1..2
drops         item=chitin count=1..3 chance=50%
bands         surface shallow
biomes        desert savanna tundra glacier
weight        10

# The back is a fixed banded gradient and the BELLY is what animates: a two-cell
# contact patch travelling head-to-tail down row 1. That is peristalsis, it is
# the one gait a legless thing has, and it is far more legible at four cells
# wide than trying to bend the back. The maw (5) appears only on the idle's
# interrupt and on the eruption, so seeing red means it is about to matter.
art.cellsW 4
art.cellsH 2
art.pal    . #6b4a24 #8a6a3c #c39a5a #e8cf9a #ff6b57
art.fps    8
art.seq  state=idle mode=ambient blinkEvery=4.2 blinkFor=0.18 |
  1231
  1..1

  1221
  1..1

  1235
  1..1
art.seq  state=move mode=phase |
  1234
  11..

  1234
  .11.

  1234
  ..11

  1234
  .11.
art.seq  state=air mode=once fps=10 |
  1235
  ....

  1234
  ....

# --- Frostmite --------------------------------------------------------------
# The first pack animal: individually trivial (7hp, 5 damage), but packSize 2..4
# means a glacier ridge produces a small skittering line of them and the fight
# is about spacing rather than about any one of them. Immune to ice so it can
# live in the material it is made of — walking over packed ice is not supposed
# to be what kills it. Held to the top 40 cells so it stays a surface-weather
# creature and does not leak into the cavern band via `shallow`.
@mob frostmite
name          Frostmite
brain         walker
maxHealth     7
contactDamage 5
attackCooldown 0.6
bodyCellsW    2
bodyCellsH    2
speed         140
chaseSpeed    260
jumpSpeed     480
aggroPx       120
aggroYPx      45
beat          1.2
immune        ice
blood         #7fd4e8
xp            2
drops         item=ice_shard count=1..2 chance=45%
bands         surface shallow
maxDepth      40
biomes        glacier tundra
packSize      2..4
weight        18

# A frost spike over a low body. The spike dulls and brightens on the breath and
# flares across both columns on the interrupt, so a LINE of these twinkles out
# of step with itself — which is what makes a pack read as several animals
# rather than as one animal drawn four times.
art.cellsW 2
art.cellsH 2
art.pal    . #2a5570 #3c6f8a #7fd4e8 #eaffff
art.fps    11
art.seq  state=idle mode=ambient blinkEvery=2.2 blinkFor=0.1 |
  .4
  32

  .3
  32

  44
  32
art.seq  state=move mode=phase |
  .4
  31

  .4
  32

  .4
  13

  .4
  32
art.seq  state=air mode=once fps=12 |
  .4
  33

  44
  .3

# --- Thornhopper ------------------------------------------------------------
# A hopper for the wet biomes, and the counterweight to the slime: same brain,
# but it fires spores instead of closing, so the danger is standing still in the
# open rather than letting it touch you. Its own spore does not hurt it
# (immune poison), which is the joke and also the reason two of them in one
# clearing is survivable.
@mob thornhopper
name          Thornhopper
brain         hopper
maxHealth     18
contactDamage 7
bodyCellsW    3
bodyCellsH    2
speed         170
jumpSpeed     600
aggroPx       150
aggroYPx      80
beat          1.3
immune        poison
blood         #7a4f9a
ranged.projectile spore
ranged.cooldown   1.9
ranged.range      165
ranged.damage     6
xp            7
value         3
drops         item=spore_sac count=1..2 chance=70%
bands         surface shallow
biomes        jungle swamp
packSize      1..2
weight        14

# The spore sac is the top-centre pixel, and it is the only thing in the sprite
# that ever changes colour: pale on the interrupt means charged. `move` is a
# three-frame shuffle rather than a phase cycle because a hopper on the ground
# is not walking, it is waiting; the real locomotion is the `air` pose, which
# tucks at launch and SPREADS at the apex and holds there for the whole arc.
art.cellsW 3
art.cellsH 2
art.pal    . #2a1b38 #3a2a4a #7a4f9a #c8ff7a #e8ffb4
art.fps    7
art.seq  state=idle mode=ambient blinkEvery=2.8 blinkFor=0.22 |
  .4.
  131

  .4.
  133

  .5.
  131
art.seq  state=move mode=loop |
  .4.
  131

  ...
  331

  .4.
  133
art.seq  state=air mode=once fps=10 |
  .4.
  .3.

  4.4
  333
